      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2009 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "A 56-year old male presenting with acute coronary syndrome was found to have a large thrombus partially including a bypass graft bare metal stent. This thrombus was removed using a filter wire. The thrombus burden was so large that it caused extension through the filter wire basket, narrowly avoiding distal embolisation."
      },
